  "body": "This immutable release resolves the four bounded findings from the independent v1.0.9 preprint referee report. It restores the positive-diagonal diffusion and singular-Jacobian hypotheses in standalone theorem exports, validates ordered certificate variables throughout the reader/generator chain, corrects the Conradi\u2013Mincheva\u2013Uecker comparison columns, and renders all rational parameter coefficients unambiguously. Release orchestration now also checks the pinned document toolchain, fails closed on TeX warnings, and regenerates PDF evidence before packaging.\n\nNo reaction topology, headline theorem, certified endpoint, exact diffusion profile, or exact current-profile datum changed. Under the pinned stack, all 39 tests, 39 verifier entrypoints, 39 optimized-Python rejection controls, the complete symbolic suite, all numerical-provenance checks, seven bundle checks, three clean submission-source builds, and the full portable replay pass. All 96 review pages were visually inspected. Historical-lineage replay still requires the five separately preserved source archives; the public replay is self-contained."
}
